### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 01 — SYSTEM HEALTH & STARTUP VERIFICATION
###
### Run these FIRST before any other test file.
### They verify the application is fully up, all subsystems are
### healthy, and the observability stack is reachable.
###
### Endpoint map:
###   GET /q/health         → combined liveness + readiness (Quarkus SmallRye)
###   GET /q/health/live    → liveness only (JVM alive)
###   GET /q/health/ready   → readiness only (dependencies healthy)
###   GET /q/metrics        → Prometheus/Micrometer scrape endpoint
###   GET /api/v1/info      → app version + build info (no auth required)
###   GET /api/v1/mcp/status→ MCP server enabled flag (auth required)
###
### Health check components (in /q/health/ready):
###   ArcClaw Podman Health  → podman socket reachable
###   ArcClaw Podman Image   → arcclaw-tool-runner image exists
###   database               → SQLite WAL connection pool live
###   sqlite-vec             → vec0 loaded (graceful degradation if absent)
###
### Expected startup log sequence (confirm in terminal before testing):
###   INFO  [AuditSchemaEnforcer] WORM triggers installed on audit_event
###   INFO  [AuditSchemaEnforcer] FTS5 memory index and triggers verified.
###   (ONE of):
###   INFO  [FtsConnectionInterceptor] sqlite-vec extension loaded successfully
###   WARN  [FtsConnectionInterceptor] sqlite-vec not found — FTS5 only
###   (attach telegram mode only):
###   INFO  [TelegramChannelRoute] routeStatus=Started
###
### Prerequisites: ArcClaw running (serve or attach mode)
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@baseUrl  = http://localhost:8080
@validKey = key-internal-cWevfEoRvstUv0PqGpf02LzDY5kPNaz1y9GSl0LZOwU=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# COMBINED HEALTH (no auth required)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [HEALTH-1] Full health check — liveness + readiness combined
# Expect 200: {"status":"UP","checks":[...all UP...]}
# status:"DOWN" at top level = at least one check failed (still HTTP 200).
GET {{baseUrl}}/q/health

###

### [HEALTH-2] Liveness probe — JVM alive, no deadlock
# Expect 200: {"status":"UP","checks":[{"name":"liveness","status":"UP"}]}
GET {{baseUrl}}/q/health/live

###

### [HEALTH-3] Readiness probe — all dependencies healthy
# Expect 200: {"status":"UP","checks":[...]}
# Each subsystem registers: database, Podman Health, Podman Image.
# sqlite-vec absent → its check shows DOWN but overall readiness remains UP
# (graceful degradation — FTS5-only mode still serves requests).
GET {{baseUrl}}/q/health/ready

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# APPLICATION INFO (no auth required)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [HEALTH-4] Application info — version, profile, build metadata
# Expect 200: {"name":"arcclaw","version":"...","profile":"dev|prod",...}
# ApiKeyAuthFilter explicitly bypasses paths starting with /api/v1/info.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/info

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# METRICS (Prometheus scrape, no auth required)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [HEALTH-5] Prometheus metrics scrape
# Expect 200: text/plain with Prometheus metric lines.
# After any agent run, look for ArcClaw-specific counters:
#   arcclaw_agent_runs_total
#   arcclaw_tokens_input_total / arcclaw_tokens_output_total
#   arcclaw_reflex_invocations_total
#   arcclaw_budget_warnings_total
#   arcclaw_audit_drop_total  ← must be 0 in normal operation
GET {{baseUrl}}/q/metrics

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MCP SERVER STATUS (auth required)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [HEALTH-6] MCP server status
# Expect 200: {"serverEnabled":true,"dynamicToolCount":0}
# 404 → arcclaw.mcp.server-enabled=false in config.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/mcp/status
Accept: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# END-TO-END SQLITE PIPELINE SMOKE TEST
# Creates session → runs agent → reads audit → verifies HMAC chain.
# Exercises the full WAL write path in one sequence.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [HEALTH-7] Create smoke-test session
# @name smokeSession
# Expect 201: {"sessionId":"xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx"}
# Failure here = SQLite WAL unreachable or Hibernate DDL failed at startup.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [HEALTH-8] Run trivial task — full pipeline smoke
# Expect 200: {"answer":"4",...}
# Exercises: SessionRegistry (Phase 64-B3), AgentLoop, GovernanceLayer,
# LLM API (Groq), AuditService, HMAC chain.
# Requires: ARCCLAW_LLM_API_KEY valid (starts with gsk_).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{smokeSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "What is 2 + 2?",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### [HEALTH-9] Verify audit events written (WORM pipeline healthy)
# Expect 200: non-empty array with CHECKPOINT_CREATED + LOOP_FINISH.
# Empty array = AsyncPersistenceEngine dropped events or AuditService failed.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/session/{{smokeSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [HEALTH-10] Verify HMAC chain integrity
# Expect 200: {"valid":true,"brokenAtId":null,"totalRows":N}
# valid:false = WORM trigger missing or ARCCLAW_AUDIT_HMAC_KEY wrong.
# After Phase 64-B1: concurrent writes protected by SessionAuditSequencer.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/{{smokeSession.response.body.sessionId}}/verify
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [HEALTH-11] Cleanup smoke session
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{smokeSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OBSERVABILITY STACK (external — requires: mise run compose:up)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [HEALTH-12] Jaeger UI reachable
# Expect 200: HTML. Open http://localhost:16686, search service="arcclaw".
GET http://localhost:16686

###

### [HEALTH-13] Prometheus targets page
# Expect 200: HTML. Open http://localhost:9090/targets — "arcclaw" must be UP.
GET http://localhost:9090/targets

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STARTUP LOG ASSERTIONS (manual — verify in terminal output)
#
#  MUST appear (any mode):
#  ✅ INFO  [AuditSchemaEnforcer] WORM triggers installed on audit_event
#  ✅ INFO  [AuditSchemaEnforcer] FTS5 memory index and triggers verified.
#  ✅ ONE of:
#       INFO  [FtsConnectionInterceptor] sqlite-vec extension loaded successfully
#       WARN  [FtsConnectionInterceptor] sqlite-vec not found — FTS5 only
#
#  In ATTACH TELEGRAM mode additionally:
#  ✅ INFO  [TelegramChannelRoute] routeStatus=Started
#
#  MUST NOT appear:
#  ❌ NullPointerException in TelegramChannelRoute
#       → Camel JMX disableJMX() silent no-op not fixed (Nuance #24)
#  ❌ ERROR in Hibernate schema validation involving "identity column"
#       → ArcClawSQLiteDialect not registered (Nuance #30)
#  ❌ DevSecretSeeder log lines in prod/staging profile
#       → Phase 64-B2 fix: @IfBuildProfile("dev") must exclude the bean
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

###
